    "legend": "Multiparametric flow analysis of peripheral blood&nbsp;monocyte subsets. CD14 and CD16 markers identify classic monocytes (cMo; CD14+, CD16&minus;), intermediate monocytes (iMo; CD14+, CD16+), and non-classic monocytes (ncMo; CD14&nbsp;low, CD16+). Their repartition in a healthy donor aged 70&nbsp;years is shown. Reactive monocytosis is associated with an increase in the iMo (and sometimes ncMo) subset. CMML typically induces an increase in the cMo fraction to &gt;&nbsp;94% of total monocytes. WBC, white blood cell.",
