    "fileId": 30748,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria of chronic myelomonocytic leukaemia (CMML)</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Joseph David Khoury",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 707.1pt; background: #daeef3; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"943\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Essential criteria</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Persistent absolute (&ge;&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/ L) and relative (&ge;&nbsp;10%) peripheral blood monocytosis</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Blasts constitute &lt;&nbsp;20% of the cells in the peripheral blood and bone marrow<sup>a</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not meeting diagnostic criteria of chronic myeloid leukaemia or other myeloproliferative neoplasms<sup>b</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">4.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Not meeting diagnostic criteria of myeloid/lymphoid neoplasms with eosinophilia and tyrosine kinase gene fusions (e.g. <em>PDGFRA</em>, <em>PDGFRB</em>, <em>FGFR1</em>, or <em>JAK2</em>)<sup>c</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Desirable criteria</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">1.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Dysplasia involving &ge;&nbsp;1&nbsp;myeloid lineages<sup>d</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">2.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Acquired clonal cytogenetic or molecular abnormality<sup>e</sup></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">3.<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Abnormal partitioning of peripheral blood monocyte subsets<sup>f</sup></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Requirements for diagnosis</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Essential criteria must be present in all cases</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">If monocytosis is &ge;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/ L: one or more desirable criteria must be met</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">If monocytosis is &lt;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/ L: desirable criteria 1 and 2 must be met</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Subtyping criteria</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Myelodysplastic CMML: WBC count &lt;&nbsp;13&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/L</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Myeloproliferative CMML: WBC count &ge;&nbsp;13&nbsp;&times;&nbsp;10<sup>9</sup>/L</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\">Subgrouping criteria</span></strong><span lang=\"EN-GB\"> (based on percentage of blasts and promonocytes)</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"break-inside: avoid; height: 10.2pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 707.1pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt; height: 10.2pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"943\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CMML-1: &lt;&nbsp;5% in peripheral blood and &lt;&nbsp;10% in bone marrow</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm 3pt 36pt; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 7pt; line-height: normal; font-family: 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span lang=\"EN-GB\">CMML-2: &ge;&nbsp;5% and &lt;&nbsp;20% in peripheral blood or &ge;&nbsp;10% and &lt;&nbsp;20% in bone marrow</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin: 3pt 0cm; font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"><span lang=\"EN-GB\">WBC, white blood cell.</span></p>\r\n<p><sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">a</span></sup><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\">Blasts</span><span lang=\"EN-GB\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;\"> and blast equivalents include myeloblasts, monoblasts, and promonocytes. <sup>b</sup>Myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPNs) can be associated with monocytosis at presentation or during the course of the disease; such cases can mimic CMML. In these instances, a documented history of MPN excludes CMML. The presence of MPN features in the bone marrow and/or a high burden of MPN-associated mutations (<em>JAK2</em>, <em>CALR</em>, or <em>MPL</em>) tends to support MPN with monocytosis rather than CMML. <sup>c</sup>Criteria for myeloid/lymphoid neoplasms with eosinophilia and tyrosine kinase gene fusions should be specifically excluded in cases with eosinophilia. <sup>d</sup>Morphological dysplasia should be present in &ge;&nbsp;10% of cells of haematopoietic lineage in the bone marrow. <sup>e</sup>See <span class=\"ID-File\" style=\"background: #ffd85b;\">&lt;&lt;#30750&gt;&gt;</span>Table&nbsp;2.13. <sup>f</sup>Based on detection of increased classic monocytes (&gt;&nbsp;94%) in the absence of known active autoimmune diseases and/or systemic inflammatory syndromes.</span></p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
